**Deduct 1 point** if the answer never raises the possibility of a NullPointerException anywhere in its discussion of the code.  

**No deduction** when the answer mentions the NPE risk at least once, regardless of how it is presented:  

* if the NPE is mentioned only inside a suggested fix or remediation advice (e.g., “add a null check to avoid a NullPointerException” or in a comment on a code snippet), it still satisfies the item;  
* if the answer frames the NPE hypothetically (e.g., “if mPrefix were null, this would throw an NPE” or “a null mPrefix would NPE here”), the requirement is met even without asserting that the null is actually possible;  
* if the answer discusses a possible NPE anywhere in its analysis of the code, even without explicitly tying it to the mPrefix access, the item is considered satisfied.  

In short, any surfacing of the NPE risk—whether as a remediation suggestion, a conditional statement, or a general NPE discussion—avoids the 1‑point deduction; only a complete absence of any NPE mention triggers the deduction.
